---
export const prerender = true;
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
---

<Content
  kicker="Legal"
  title="Refunds & Cancellations"
  description="How refunds, cancellations, and billing disputes work on Saathum, including app-store purchases and the rules for tokens."
  image="/og/refunds.png"
  lead="What can be refunded on Saathum, what cannot, and how to raise a billing problem."
  updated="2026-08-28"
  helpHref="/help/billing/refunds"
>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.c2a40a66132679cc">This policy explains how refunds and cancellations work on Saathum — our creator marketplace,
    paid live streaming, and paid 1:1 video sessions. It sits alongside
    our</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-refunds.4afa55bf7aec7ddc" href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, <a data-i18n="web-refunds.188dc350278985ab" href="/tokens">Tokens &amp; Wallet</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.16047a3f9597e500">policy, and</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-refunds.5e2a4b33bff1936b" href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.2c0560d6168d330b">page.</ui-copy>
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.0922ebe046cfa13d" id="status">1. Who you are dealing with</h2>

  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.65e081354f24d9d0">Your agreement is with Saathum, under the laws
    described in our</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-refunds.4afa55bf7aec7ddc" href="/terms">Terms of Service</a><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.5568f94f0e161ed0">. If anything on this page is unclear,
    email</ui-copy> <a href="mailto:support@saathum.com">support@saathum.com</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.6ce88ccb509cc7ba">before you pay.</ui-copy>
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.7ba63bf41f0df2dc">2. Token values and payment records</h2>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.65bcdb28bb2fdfbd">Saathum uses</ui-copy> <strong data-i18n="web-refunds.1333886bf7b67378">1 Token = ₹1</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.0d7350d4ced7e0de">as the fixed customer-facing value in India. The
      payment snapshot records the exact Token amount attached to that payment.</ui-copy>
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px">
      <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.8c960f8ccf5397cc">If a payment or booking is reversed, the wallet reversal is for the</ui-copy> <strong data-i18n="web-refunds.50cdbd5ff69d998d">exact token amount
      recorded in the immutable payment snapshot</strong><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.93e70db03769f46f">. We do not reprice a reversal using a later
      later rate. For a billing problem, email</ui-copy>
      <a href="mailto:support@saathum.com">support@saathum.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.f00e6edeeb4da04f">3. Token refunds and reversals</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.7409d8ee5a9921ab">When you top up, the payment is recorded with the
    exact Token amount. Tokens are the in-app unit used to pay for AI features and services. The fixed
    customer-facing value is</ui-copy> <strong data-i18n="web-refunds.1333886bf7b67378">1 Token = ₹1</strong><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.b29a618cc32248d2"> in India.</ui-copy>
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong data-i18n="web-refunds.5f8e3bc8d30ccf61">Once purchased or converted, tokens are not automatically refundable</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.ef2da13cf7196b98">— except where a
      refund is required by applicable law, or by the billing policy of the app store you bought
      through (Google Play or Apple). Nothing in this policy limits rights you have that cannot be
      waived under consumer law where you live.</ui-copy>
    </p>
    <p>
      <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.cef3f289c93f56af">A qualifying refund or booking cancellation returns the</ui-copy> <strong data-i18n="web-refunds.5f9af22f4ff8bf4e">exact token amount recorded for
      the original transaction</strong><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.0b12c2486c218e5b">. Withdrawal and cash-redemption semantics are not yet
      available. See section 6 and</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-refunds.aba115e7791e41dc" href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.df28f6ee1536de9e">4. Purchases made through an app store</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.5bb3b1635148b63c">
    If you bought a top-up or subscription inside the Android or iOS app, the payment was taken by
    the app store, not by us. Refunds for those purchases are handled by the store under its own
    policy and timelines:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong data-i18n="web-refunds.027b1684683ad703">Google Play</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.1e553d43da48f92f">— request a refund through your Google Play order history or
      Google Play support.</ui-copy></li>
    <li><strong data-i18n="web-refunds.f223faa96f229162">Apple</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.3706062e4c4e25f0">— request a refund through Apple's "Report a Problem" process or
      Apple Support.</ui-copy></li>
  </ul>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.4113c67fa6ac3d7b">
    We cannot reverse a store charge on your behalf. If the store approves a refund, we may reverse
    the exact corresponding token amount from the immutable payment snapshot. If those tokens have already been spent, your
    balance may go to zero and your account may be restricted until the position is corrected.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.1c33dc93470f5482">5. Cancelling a subscription vs consuming tokens</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.7920dab051e7fde1">
    These are two different things:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong data-i18n="web-refunds.50e833ed07174399">Cancelling a recurring plan</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.7d334ee918fc3bdd">stops future charges. Cancel it wherever you
      set it up — usually the app store's subscriptions screen. Cancelling generally does not
      refund a period you have already paid for, and access normally continues until the end of the
      current period.</ui-copy></li>
    <li><strong data-i18n="web-refunds.e7cc72cd8a98e9ac">Spending tokens</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.3930308eb0df0823">is immediate and is treated as consumption of the service.
      A token spent on an AI feature, a marketplace purchase, or a consultation is used up at that
      point.</ui-copy></li>
  </ul>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.430ce8c5629aca8c">
    Cancelling a plan does not by itself remove tokens already in your balance.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.7168249ec1feb78a">6. Unused vs consumed tokens</h2>
  <p>
    <strong data-i18n="web-refunds.b803e56ff96e2511">Consumed tokens</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.1fca6b8deef40e20">— tokens already spent on a delivered feature or service — are
    not refundable, except where required by law.</ui-copy>
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong data-i18n="web-refunds.220a769564b58615">Unused tokens</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.df1465468d492d95">remain in your wallet as tokens. Withdrawal semantics are not yet
    available. Where a refund or reversal applies, it uses the exact token amount in the original
    transaction snapshot, not a later rate. See</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-refunds.aba115e7791e41dc" href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.39af8479048587d0">7. Marketplace purchases and consultations</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.93dfac6b2237f82f">
    The marketplace and live consultancy connect you with other users who provide digital services.
    We may apply the following where a booking or order goes wrong:
  </p>
  <h3 data-i18n="web-refunds.52ea24f1ec02cfb1">Cancellations</h3>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.157181308ce8ff48">
    A booking cancelled before the agreed start time may be eligible for a return of tokens to your
    balance, subject to the cancellation terms shown on the listing at the time of booking and to
    our review.
  </p>
  <h3 data-i18n="web-refunds.d9a54d4cc678f9d0">No-shows</h3>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.3610bc7df03c6585">
    If the provider does not attend a booked session, you may raise it with us and we may return the
    tokens to your balance. If the customer does not attend, the session may be treated as delivered
    and the tokens as consumed.
  </p>
  <h3 data-i18n="web-refunds.c14b6dcc519bdb26">Failure to deliver</h3>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.8ec7d72384e5dcd4">If a provider does not deliver what the listing described, tell us at</ui-copy>
    <a href="mailto:support@saathum.com">support@saathum.com</a><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.f64b0c51a21730ca">. We may review the order, withhold or
    reverse the provider's earnings, and return tokens to your balance where we consider it
    appropriate. We are not the provider of the underlying service and do not guarantee any
    particular outcome.</ui-copy>
  </p>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.137d639919881e8a">Any resolution we make is normally in</ui-copy> <strong data-i18n="web-refunds.f955d1c7f89560a7">tokens returned to your balance</strong><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.96ea80e29da57e5b">, not a
    payment back to your card or bank.</ui-copy>
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.42aa68a78aee19b1">8. Chargebacks</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.a4a3815d81b25e07">
    If you believe a charge is wrong, please contact us first — a chargeback is slower for everyone
    and may restrict your account while it is open. Where a chargeback or payment reversal is raised
    against your account, we may suspend the account, freeze the token balance, and reverse tokens
    linked to the disputed payment. We may decline further top-ups from a payment method with an
    unresolved dispute.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.70ca1abb18850cf2">9. Fraud and abuse</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.fff5319b8ff24b32">We may refuse, reverse, or hold a refund where we reasonably suspect fraud, abuse of promotional
    credit, or a breach of our</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-refunds.4afa55bf7aec7ddc" href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.6a536903e1ef3309">10. How to raise a billing issue</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.969ccbd3cf6300ec">Email</ui-copy> <a href="mailto:support@saathum.com">support@saathum.com</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.1443ea783e5df833">from the address on your account
    and include:</ui-copy>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li data-i18n="web-refunds.a789ff18d1a1a472">your Saathum handle or registered email;</li>
    <li data-i18n="web-refunds.5f03272ad75778bf">the date and Indian-rupee amount of the charge, plus the Token amount if shown;</li>
    <li data-i18n="web-refunds.a48c885cee066df3">whether you paid through Google Play, Apple, or another method;</li>
    <li data-i18n="web-refunds.489a37bc03d8e121">the order, booking, or transaction reference if you have one;</li>
    <li data-i18n="web-refunds.e8fda4dd92924bea">a short description of what went wrong.</li>
  </ul>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.0bf4d1fa126cf10e">
    We will look into it and respond. We cannot promise a specific turnaround, and any refund we do
    make is returned by the same method that took the payment where possible.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.f5007dc76b66f358">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-refunds.73ee27295f2ed9be">
    We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the updated version here and revise
    the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-refunds.5adadc207219605c">12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.31f99beb659dec48">Billing and payout questions:</ui-copy> <a href="mailto:support@saathum.com">support@saathum.com</a><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.a2bd067f82126b7a">. General
    enquiries:</ui-copy> <a href="mailto:support@saathum.com">support@saathum.com</a><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.966163e6c8882917">. Privacy questions:</ui-copy>
    <a href="mailto:support@saathum.com">support@saathum.com</a><ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.bf2fb03dedc02906">. See also our</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-refunds.4afa55bf7aec7ddc" href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-refunds.6201111b83a0cb5b">and</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-refunds.506ff394621596dd" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</Content>
